// ---- lapis-bridge.mjs
/* Lapis desk bridge
   A browser page cannot send UDP/TCP to a mixing console. This small program runs on your laptop,
   listens ONLY on 127.0.0.1 and relays OSC messages from Lapis to a console on your local network.

   Safety:
   - pairing code: printed at start; Lapis must send it with every request (X-Lapis-Key)
   - consoles on private addresses only (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 169.254/16, 127/8)
   - drivers can only read and write channel names and colours, and 48V (X32 / M32, X Air, DiGiCo) when the request
     carries an explicit confirmation (never faders, mutes or gain)
   - desk snapshot recall (DiGiCo) only when "Allow desk snapshots" is on in the Bridge panel (off by default)
   - QLab (qlab.mjs): on this computer or a private address; GO, stop, panic and the playhead; writes MIDI trigger cues only when asked (edit passcode);
     read-only mode blocks every QLab command
   - crew share link (share.mjs): off by default; when on, a second, read-only web server on port 52410 serves the last
     published paperwork at a random token address for phones on the same network. The control port stays on 127.0.0.1.
   - the assistant (ai.mjs): API keys stay in ~/.lapis/ai.json; requests go only to Anthropic, OpenAI, Google's
     Gemini API or a local Ollama; the assistant changes the show in Lapis, never a device
   Usage: node bridge/lapis-bridge.mjs [--port 52400] [--key CODE]            Node 18+ */
